{number: 149}
{title: Jesus Calls Us}
{key: Bb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Bb] Jesus calls us; o'er the [Eb] tumult
Of our [Bb] life's wild, restless [F7] sea,
[Bb] Day by day His sweet voice [Eb] soundeth,
Saying, [Bb] "Christian, [F7] follow [Bb] Me.“
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Bb] Jesus calls us from the [Eb] worship
Of the [Bb] vain world's golden [F7] store;
[Bb] From each idol that would [Eb] keep us,
Saying, [Bb] "Christian, [F7] love Me [Bb] more."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
In [Bb] our joys and in our [Eb] sorrows,
Days of [Bb] toil and hours of [F7] ease,
Still [Bb] He calls, in cares and [Eb] pleasures,
"That we [Bb] love Him [F7] more than [Bb] these.“
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[Bb] Jesus calls us: by Thy [Eb] mercies,
Saviour, [Bb] may we hear Thy [F7] call,
Give [Bb] our hearts to Thine o-[Eb] bedience,
Serve and [Bb] love Thee [F7] best of [Bb] all.
{end_of_verse}
